    "notes": "Worked example. Three cooked meals containing coriander (ingredient 101), rated 2, 1, 1 stars, each cooking event in the same transaction as its meal log; exposure shares 2/4, 1/4, 1/2 weight the updates and the 60-day cook-rating half-life decays the posterior between them. A fourth, unrated cook of the stir-fry is followed two days later by recipe_rated (rating 3, cookEventId merge at strength 1.0), plus a save (reward 0.75, no slate) and a skip of the coriander recipe against the slate that showed it (reward 0.15). The learned layer stays small: coriander's contribution is -0.546217. An active pin (pinnedValue -8) on coriander dominates learning and binds GLOBAL_CLAMP on both coriander recipes (learnedContributionRaw below -8, learnedContribution exactly -8), pushing them under the tied featureless pair: R2 and R4 both ruleScore 60.0 and separate only by the rank tiebreak (recipe id ascending). cuisine:indian and technique:stirfry each have one cooked recipe and hide from the profile as thin evidence.",
